  "text": "أسلandscape Hospital has 2 plants. Each plant produces 4 things per day, and these equations give the total number of things produced per day (x) depending on the days (t) that the hospital has plants:\n- Equation 1: x = 2lot ∙ t\n- Equation 2: x = 24 - 2r i\n\nFind the value of x when the hospital operates 10 days.\n🚆 To find the value of \\( x \\) when the hospital operates for 10 days using both equations, we need to understand that both equations represent the same physical situation and therefore should give identical results. Let's start by checking the consistency of these equations for the specific case of operating for 10 days (\\( t = 10 \\)).\n\nFor both equations:\n- Equation 1: \\( x = 2(t \\cdot lot) \\)\n- Equation 2: \\( x = 24 - 2t \\)\n\nFirst, we substitute \\( t = 10 \\) into each equation.\n\nStarting with Equation 1:\n\\[\nx = 2(t \\cdot lot)\n\\]\nBut we don't have the value of \\( lot \\). Perhaps there was a mistake in the notation. If we assume \\( lot \\) is a typo and meant to be interpreted as \\( l \\), then the correct equation for Equation 1 would be:\n\\[\nx = 2(l \\cdot t)\n\\]\nHowever, since we don't know \\( l \\), we'll proceed with Equation 2 to find \\( x \\).\n\nSubstituting \\( t = 10 \\) into Equation 2:\n\\[\nx = 24 - 2t\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 24 - 2(10)\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 24 - 20\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 4\n\\]\n\nSince both equations are setup to represent the same physical situation, and they give different results based on \\( lot \\), I made the assumption that the notation might have a typo or that there's an oversight. Based on the information provided and assuming Equation 2 is the correct one for our context, the value of \\( x \\) when the hospital operates for 10 days is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
